| description = Primes all enemies in an expanding radius with volatile antimatter. Press the ability to slow down enemy movement, hold the ability to speed them up.
| strength = 150 / 300 / 500 / 800 (explosion {{D|Blast}} damage)<br>35% / 40% / 45% / 50% (slow/speed-up)
| range = 6 / 7 / 8 / 10 m (explosion radius)
| duration = 2 / 3 / 4 / 6 s (wave duration)<br>10 / 15 / 20 / 30 s (prime duration)
| misc = 5 m (starting wave radius)<br>5 m/s (wave speed)<br>20% ({{D|Blast}} status chance)<br>+100% ([[Damage Vulnerability]])<br>75% (slow/speed cap)
| info = *Nova expends {{Stat|Ability Efficiency|icon=only}}'''100''' [[energy]] to unleash a radial wave of antimatter particles. The wave starts <u>'''5'''</u> meters from Nova and propagates at a speed of <u>'''5'''</u> meters per second for {{Stat|Ability Duration|icon=only}}'''2 / 3 / 4 / 6''' seconds before dissipating. All enemies in range are coated in antimatter that destabilizes their molecular structure for {{Stat|Ability Duration|icon=only}}'''10 / 15 / 20 / 30''' seconds.
**Wave Radius is calculated as:
**:{{MathText|Wave Radius {{eql}} 5 + (5 {{mul}} (Wave Duration {{mul}} Ability Duration))}}
***For example, Molecular Prime at rank 3 with 150% Ability Duration will have wave radius of:
***:{{Math|5 + (5 {{mul}} (6 {{mul}} 150%))|mt=y}} meters
**If Nova dies or leaves the mission, enemies will immediately lose their primed state.
**A maximum of <u>'''5'''</u> Molecular Prime waves can exist at a time. Recasting the ability will remove the oldest wave.
*'''Tap''' the ability key to unleash a '''{{D|Slow}}''' wave. '''Hold''' the ability key to unleash a '''Speed-Up''' wave. Primed enemies have their action speed increased or decreased by {{Stat|Ability Strength|icon=only}}'''35% / 40% / 45% / 50%''', receive <u>'''+100%'''</u> [[Damage Vulnerability]], and detonate upon death dealing {{Stat|Ability Strength|icon=only}}'''150 / 300 / 500 / 800''' {{D|Blast}} damage with <u>'''20%'''</u> [[Status Chance]] to enemies within {{Stat|Ability Range|icon=only}}'''6 / 7 / 8 / 10''' meters.
**Slow/speed-up debuff is capped at <u>'''75%'''</u>, achievable with 150% {{Stat|Ability Strength}}.
**Explosion damage has <u>'''60%'''</u> linear [[Damage Falloff]].
**Each explosion can cause the subsequent death and detonation of nearby enemies, resulting in a chain reaction.
*'''Ability Synergy:''' Enemies killed by Nova while slowed [[Nova/Abilities#Passive|passively]] have a <u>'''15%'''</u> chance to drop a [[Pickup#Orbs|Health Orb]], while enemies killed while sped-up have a <u>'''15%'''</u> chance to drop an [[Pickups#Orb|Energy Orb]].
*Molecular Prime does '''not''' stack from multiple Novas.
<div class="mw-collapsible mw-collapsed">
<div style="font-weight:bold;line-height:2;">Unique Interactions With Explosions</div>
<div class="mw-collapsible-content">
*Due to Molecular Prime explosions counting as a [[Weapons|Weapon Hit]],  it can cause the ability to inherit certain traits from the [[Weapon]]/[[Ability]] that dealt the killing blow to the primed enemy which can all be propagated through chain reactions of explosions. Some such effects are:
**Killing a primed enemy with {{A|Demonium}} Runes, {{A|Resupply}} Ammo Packs, {{A|Silken Stride}}, {{A|Toxic Lash}}, {{A|Xata's Whisper}} active will cause the explosion to do another instance of damage.
**Molecular Prime explosions from Melee Kills will be able to [[Stealth|Stealth Hit]], thus benefitting from the [[Stealth|Stealth Damage Bonus]] (+700%)
**Killing a primed enemy can cause the explosion to trigger equipped [[Arcanes|Weapon Arcanes]].
***On melee kill, the explosion benefits from {{Arcane|Melee Influence}} while it is active.
***On secondary kill, the explosion can deal increased Overguard Damage if {{Arcane|Secondary Fortifier}} is equipped.
***On Molecular Prime hit that causes Status with {{Arcane|Secondary Encumber}} equipped, you have a 24% chance to proc another random Status Effect.
***The explosion from killing a primed enemy with a your Primary/Secondary/Melee will cause Molecular Prime kills to stack Merciless Arcanes ({{Arcane|Primary Merciless|Primary}}/{{Arcane|Secondary Merciless|Secondary}}) as well as Dexterity Arcanes({{Arcane|Primary Dexterity|Primary}}/{{Arcane|Secondary Dexterity|Secondary}}) Respectively.
***Kills from your Primary/Secondary will cause Molecular Prime Headshot Kills to stack Deadhead Arcanes ({{Arcane|Primary Deadhead|Primary}}/{{Arcane|Secondary Deadhead|Secondary}}) Respectively.
**The explosions can also benefit from select [[Mods|Weapon Mods]]. Some such mods that apply are:
***[[Faction Damage Bonus|Faction Damage Bonuses]] from the killing [[Weapon]] will apply to explosion damage.
***[[Elementalist Mods|Elementalist Mods]] will apply to the Molecular Prime explosions {{D|Blast}} procs.
*** {{M|Combustion Beam}} will trigger on Molecular Prime kills.
*** {{M|Energizing Shot|Energizing}}/{{M|Mending Shot}} will trigger on Molecular Prime hitting the respective orb type.
*On Kill with the [[Weapon]], Molecular Prime explosions gain the following [[Weapon]] traits:
**[[Weapon Augment Mods]]:
***{{Weapon|Argonak}}: While using a [[Dagger]] with an {{Weapon|Argonak}} equipped with {{M|Amalgam Argonak Metal Auger}}, the resulting explosions will strip 6 armor from every enemy it hits.
***{{Weapon|Daikyu}}({{Weapon|Daikyu Prime|Prime}}): While using a [[Nikana]] with a {{Weapon|Daikyu}}({{Weapon|Daikyu Prime|Prime}}) equipped with {{M|Amalgam Daikyu Target Acquired}}, the resulting explosions will gain 3% lifesteal.
***{{Weapon|Hate}}: While {{M|Burning Hate}} is equipped, the explosions will cause Status Vulnerability when hitting enemies affected by {{D|Heat}}.
***{{Weapon|Sobek}}/{{Weapon|Jat Kittag}}/{{Weapon|Detron}}({{Weapon|Mara Detron|Mara}}/{{Weapon|Tenet Detron|Tenet}}): Kills from Molecular Prime will trigger the following mods for the respective [[Weapons]]: {{M|Acid Shells}}, {{M|Vulcan Blitz}}, {{M|Thermagnetic Shells}}
***{{Weapon|Furax}}({{Weapon|Mk1-Furax|Mk1}}/{{Weapon|Furax Wraith|Wraith}}): Kills from Molecular Prime with {{M|Amalgam Furax Body Count}} equipped will prime {{D|Blast}} and stagger enemies.
***{{Weapon|Bronco}}({{Weapon|Bronco Prime|Prime}}): Explosion hits with {{M|Dizzying Rounds}} equipped will stagger enemies and open them up to finishers.
***{{Weapon|Furis}}({{Weapon|Mk1-Furis|Mk1}}): Explosion hits with {{M|Winds of Purity}} equipped will gain 20% lifesteal.
***{{Weapon|Catabolyst}}({{Weapon|Coda Catabolyst|Coda}}): Explosion kills while {{M|Critical Mutation}} is equipped will stack Critical Chance & Damage Buffs.
**[[Passives/Weapon|Weapon Passives]]:
***{{Weapon|Enkaus}}: Molecular Prime hits on enemies within the insta-kill threshold will instakill them. Additionally, when Molecular Prime hits inked enemies, {{Weapon|Enkaus}} will regain ammo.
***{{Weapon|Pathocyst}}({{Weapon|Coda Pathocyst|Coda}}): Molecular Prime Hits spawn Maggots/Miasmites respectively.
***{{Weapon|Reconifex}}: Perfectly timed reloads give a {{D|Heat}} Magazine, allowing Molecular Prime to additionally proc {{D|Heat}} Status.
***{{Weapon|Venato Prime}}: Molecular Prime Status Effects will inflict {{D|Tau}} Status.
***{{Weapon|Spinnerex}}: Molecular Prime hits grant the enemies a 10% chance per {{D|Toxin}} Stack to detonate on death.
***{{Weapon|Rakta Dark Dagger}}: Damage on enemies affected by {{D|Radiation}} status generates shields.
***{{Weapon|Secura Lecta}}: Explosion kills will yield 2x [[Credits]].
***{{Weapon|Heliocor}}({{Weapon|Synoid Heliocor|Synoid}}): Explosion kills will perform a [[Codex|Codex Scan]] on enemies.
***{{Weapon|Amanata}}: Explosion benefits from Status Damage, additive to [[Elementalist Mods]]
***{{Weapon|Dorrclave}}: Explosion guarantees status on initial enemy hit, not to surrounding enemies, removes stacks of buff.
***{{Weapon|Evensong}}: Explosion inflicts 7 stacks of {{D|Puncture}} on enemies (bypassing the normal limit of 5), making them deal 0 damage to you.
***{{Weapon|Trumna}}({{Weapon|Trumna Prime|Prime}}): Explosion kills generate charges for the Alternate Fire and can generate Alternate Fire from its own kills as long as you bounce the projectile once.
***{{Weapon|Pyrana Prime}}: 3 Rapid explosion kills will activate the Akimbo Mode.
***{{Weapon|Tatsu}}({{Weapon|Tatsu Prime|Prime}}): Molecular Prime kills originating from the Tatsu Prime will stack the charges.
**[[Incarnon|Incarnon Evolutions]]:
***{{Weapon|Phenmor}}:
**** Evolution III (Executioner's Fortune) equipped will cause the [[Weapon]] to have a chance to refill its magazine. Seen as it is a refill and not a reload, it will keep Elemental Ammo Packs from {{A|Resupply}}
**** Evolution V (Devouring Attrition) equipped will cause the explosion to have a 50% chance to deal +2000% damage on non-critical hits.
**** Explosion Headshots with Evolution V (Lingering Judgment) equipped will cause the explosion to deal 50% Headshot Damage for 8s.
***{{Weapon|Laetum}}:
**** Hits with Evolution IV (Caput Mortuum) equipped will cause the explosion to deal 50% more Headshot Damage.
**** Kills with Evolution V (Devouring Attrition) equipped will cause the explosion to have a 50% chance to deal +2000% damage on non-critical hits.
**** Hits with Evolution V (Overwhelming Attrition) equipped will stack the perk.
***{{Weapon|Felarx}}:
**** Kills with Evolution V (Devastating Attrition) equipped will cause the explosions ot have a 50% chance to deal +2000% damage on non-critical hits.
***{{Weapon|Dual Ichor}}:
**** Evolution I will cause the explosions to create a Toxin Damage field while Incarnon Form is active.
**** Evolution II will cause the explosions to generate combo if hitting enemies affected by {{D|Toxin}}.
***{{Weapon|Okina}}({{Weapon|Okina Prime|Prime}}):
**** Evolution I will cause the explosions to generate spectral daggers while Incarnon Form is active.
**** Evolution II (Seeing Red) will cause the explosions to generate combo if hitting enemies affected by {{D|Slash}}
***{{Weapon|Lato}}({{Weapon|Lato Vandal|Vandal}}/{{Weapon|Lato Prime|Prime}}):
**** Evolution III (Exact Penance) will cause the explosions to have a 50% chance to reload the [[Weapon]].
***{{Weapon|Ceramic Dagger}}({{Weapon|Ack & Brunt}}):
**** Evolution III/IV (Rogue Readiness) will cause the explosions to have a 50% chance to reload your Primary and Secondary [[Weapon|Weapons]].
*Misc:
**Explosion radius is '''not''' affected by mods such as {{M|Fulmination}}.
