{{clr}}
| tips = *Enemies that spawn after the initial cast but are within the expanding wave are immediately primed.
*Speed-Up (hold cast) is particularly useful in [[Defense]] missions to force enemy waves to come out faster.
*Recasting the ability while it is still active will allow a wider average coverage, as by the time the first cast collapses, the recast will have already spread some distance.
*Speed-Up works on Eximus and other units protected by [[Overguard]], although the slow does not.
*Molecular Prime works incredibly well in conjunction with {{A|Antimatter Drop}}, weakening a boss, or killing entire legions of enemies by triggering an explosion.
*It should be noted that the slow effect for Molecular Prime stacks with other abilities that slow. When used alongside {{WF|Frost}}'s {{A|Snow Globe}}, or other effects such as {{D|Cold}} elemental mods, this ability is also capable of bringing enemies and bosses to a grinding halt, dramatically slowing them and easing the capability of landing headshots for the whole team.
*Synergizes well with {{WF|Nyx}}'s {{A|Chaos}} as units will attack each other dealing double damage, weakening every individual until someone dies and causes a series of chain explosions that can kill the entire group.
*Synergizes well with {{WF|Saryn}}'s {{A|Spores}} {{D|Corrosive}} proc by first spreading and weakening every individual armored unit, then causing a series of chain explosions when a single one dies.
*Synergizes well with {{WF|Loki}}'s augment mod {{M|Irradiating Disarm}} for his fourth ability {{A|Radial Disarm}} which creates an AoE disarm and {{D|Radiation}} proc as units will attack each other dealing double damage, weakening every individual until someone dies and causes a series of chain explosions that can kill the entire group.
*Primed enemies' bodies visibly dissolve after death by detonation, but they are actually hidden and not yet removed, thus allowing {{WF|Nekros}} to cast {{A|Desecrate}}.
*Speed alteration does not affect the interval between tick damage of status effect nor their duration. 
